<DocsPageSectionTitle>
    Best Practices
</DocsPageSectionTitle>

<DocsPageSubsectionTitle IncludeInToc="false">
    Keep Context Compact
</DocsPageSubsectionTitle>

<DocsPageParagraph>
    Addons work best for brief, familiar context such as currency symbols, units, or URL prefixes. Keep the field's actual label outside the addon, and avoid addon content that competes with the editable value or leaves too little input space on smaller screens.
</DocsPageParagraph>

<DocsPageSubsectionTitle IncludeInToc="false">
    Field Meaning
</DocsPageSubsectionTitle>

<DocsPageParagraph>
    Treat addon text as presentation rather than part of the submitted value, and validate the complete value in application code. When an addon contains a button, describe a clear action and provide an accessible label if the button uses only an icon.
</DocsPageParagraph>

